Cosmo APE VFS hunks applied to SQLCipher *source* at amalgamation time.

Do not edit sqlite3.c by hand. Do not put these edits in the SQLCipher
git tree (keep that rebaseable against sqlcipher/sqlcipher).

  patches/cosmo-vfs.patch
    src/os_unix.c
      - HAVE_PREAD/PWRITE when __COSMOPOLITAN__
      - msync() mapped pages in unixSync (Windows FlushViewOfFile;
        OpenBSD mmap/pread coherence)
      - save/restore errno in unixGetTempname and unixAccess
    src/sqliteInt.h
      - SQLITE_MAX_MMAP_SIZE on __COSMOPOLITAN__

Not included (on purpose, for upgrade ease):

  - F2FS batch-atomic ioctls / IsLinux()  — cherrybean does not set
    SQLITE_ENABLE_BATCH_ATOMIC_WRITE; Cosmo vanilla sqlite does. Add
    both the flag and runtime IsLinux() guards together if you want it.
  - full_fsync F_FULLFSYNC rewrite — Cosmo libc fsync/fdatasync already
    do XNU F_FULLFSYNC and Windows FlushFileBuffers.
  - Cosmo-style include rewrite (libc/dce.h, linux/f2fs.h, …)

Refresh after a SQLCipher bump:

  git -C ../sqlcipher/cherrybean merge   # or rebase onto upstream
  third_party/sqlcipher/upgrade.sh
  # if patch -p1 fails, edit cosmo-vfs.patch against the new files
  grep cherrybean-cosmo-vfs third_party/sqlcipher/sqlite3.c
